  "body": "Undercutting and form cutters have no tool kind.\n\n**Where:** `ToolKind` (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs:23`) has no lollipop (undercut ball), back-chamfer, dovetail, concave corner-rounding, slitting saw, keyseat, or form cutter. The spun cutter outline (`cutter`, #93) is display-only: \"nothing a generator or law reads changes\" (`crates/app/src/project/file.rs`, `ToolDto::cutter` doc).\n\n**Effect:** these common tools (corner rounding is one of the most common finishing tools on small mills) can't be used in operations. A tool library build left dozens of each out.\n\n**Fix sketch:**\n- First: a generic \"form cutter\" kind whose spun outline IS read by the generators, the sim and the gouge/collision laws. That covers corner rounding, dovetail, lollipop and back-chamfer as profiles.\n- Then specialised ops: undercut contour, slot with a slitting saw.\n\nEffort: max.\n\n**Done means:** a corner-rounding cutter rounds a top edge in a 2D contour op that verifies clean; its outline is used by the sim; pinned.\n",
